1. Troubleshooting subnet issues involves identifying IP exhaustion or CIDR overlaps via cloud dashboards (like VPC consoles) and CLI commands 

2.Fix insufficient IPs by adding secondary CIDR blocks, resizing subnets, or freeing up unused Elastic Network Interfaces (ENIs). 

3.Resolve overlapping CIDRs by reallocating subnets, using CGNAT ranges, or implementing NAT gateways between conflicting
 
4.Investigate which workloads, services (e.g., App Runner, EKS), or resources are consuming excessive IPs.

